      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "node::W2914139079"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed process decomposes hydride precursors under vacuum and then uses cold isostatic pressing and extrusion.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hydride decomposition should occur under ultra-high vacuum below 10^-6 torr or inert gas containing less than 10 ppm O2.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heating at 10–50 °C/min to 600–800 °C ensures complete hydrogen release without rapid oxidation.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Extrusion should be conducted at 1000–1200 °C and a strain rate of 0.001–0.01 s^-1.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "node::W2914139079"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The adapted process retains a single-phase BCC solid solution.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "node::W2914139079",
        "node::W2020462182"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Avoiding brittle alpha-HCP phases helps retain the BCC structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxygen uptake induces precipitation of detrimental intermetallic phases such as Al-Zr or Ti-O phases.",
